## Power of Three Problem Solution in Java

### Problem Statement

Given an integer `n`, return `true` if it is a power of three. Otherwise, return `false`.

### Solution

We will provide two solutions: one using a loop and another without using loops or recursion.

#### Solution with Loop

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        }
        return n == 1;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(27));  // true
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(0));   // false
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(-1));  // false
    }
}
```

#### Solution without Loop/Recursion

We can use the mathematical property that if `n` is a power of three, then `log(n)` divided by `log(3)` should be an integer. We will check if this quotient is an integer.

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        double result = Math.log(n) / Math.log(3);
        return Math.abs(result - Math.round(result)) < 1e-9;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(27));  // true
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(0));   // false
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(-1));  // false
    }
}
```

In the above code, we compare the absolute difference between `result` and its rounded value to a very small number (`1e-9`) to account for floating-point precision errors.

Alternatively, we can also use the fact that the maximum power of three within the given range is `3^19 = 1162261467`. So, we can check if `n` is a divisor of this number.

```java
public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        return n > 0 && 1162261467 % n == 0;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(27));  // true
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(0));   // false
        System.out.println(solution.isPowerOfThree(-1));  // false
    }
}
```

This solution is more efficient and straightforward. It directly checks if `n` is a power of three by verifying if it is a divisor of `1162261467`.

